    {
      "jobId": "2df6a64e-6ce8-49f9-876a-a37cd9dcd52e",
      "question": "As of 2026-09-30, how many denied claims that have not been appealed are still inside their payer's first-level appeal window, and what is the billed amount by payer?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-03T04:18:28.983234Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-03T04:18:38.362044Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "As of **2026-09-30**, there are **25 denied claims** that have not been appealed and are still within their payer's first-level appeal window, totaling **$106,658.13** in billed amounts.\n\n| Payer | Denied claims not appealed (in window) | Total billed amount (USD) |\n|-------|----------------------------------------|---------------------------|\n| Cascade Mutual | 1 | $315.25 |\n| Evergreen Health Plan | 2 | $252.54 |\n| Medicaid | 7 | $30,795.35 |\n| Medicare | 11 | $73,882.29 |\n| Northstar Advantage | 4 | $1,412.70 |\n| **Total** | **25** | **$106,658.13** |\n\n**Appeal windows used** (from the Payer Contract Summary RHN-CON-009): Medicare 120 days, Northstar Advantage 60 days, Medicaid 90 days, Evergreen Health Plan 180 days, Cascade Mutual 60 days. Self-pay has no appeal window and is excluded. [1] [2]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — 2 documents — evidence `hermes-receipt:3fe15aa4ce55db0a66ef46319aedd2b5c4f42ae793f585419568e93d4fe0ddd3`\n- [2] Structured retrieval result — healthcare_clinical — evidence `hermes-receipt:44aaa829119c49afb3cd887c152ff705fe05bf7505c8c558ccd92daec8fae84d`",
