                "title": "payer_contract_summary.docx",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Payer Contract Summary: Denials and Appeals\n2. How the appeal window works\nThe first-level appeal window runs in calendar days from the date on the payer's denial notice (the adjudication date in the claims system). A claim is appealable on a given date if that date is on or before the notice date plus the window. An appeal that arrives after the window closes is rejected as untimely and the balance is written off. The window is the same for every denial reason, including \"Prior authorization missing\", \"Medical necessity\" and \"Coding error\".",
                "metadata": {
                  "parser": "docling-docx",
                  "file_id": "f-e59444b13b07179b",
                  "file_name": "payer_contract_summary.docx",
                  "citation": "payer_contract_summary.docx",
                  "headings": "Payer Contract Summary: Denials and Appeals › 2. How the appeal window works",
                  "labels": [
                    "text"
                  ]
                }
              },
