                "snippet": "Denials and prior authorization\nMedicare, Claims adjudicated in Q2 = 238. Medicare, Denied = 14. Medicare, Denial rate = 5.9%. Northstar Advantage, Claims adjudicated in Q2 = 122. Northstar Advantage, Denied = 11. Northstar Advantage, Denial rate = 9.0%. Medicaid, Claims adjudicated in Q2 = 76. Medicaid, Denied = 7. Medicaid, Denial rate = 9.2%. Evergreen Health Plan, Claims adjudicated in Q2 = 81. Evergreen Health Plan, Denied = 5. Evergreen Health Plan, Denial rate = 6.2%. Cascade Mutual, Claims adjudicated in Q2 = 91. Cascade Mutual, Denied = 6. Cascade Mutual, Denial rate = 6.6%. Self-pay, Claims adjudicated in Q2 = 24. Self-pay, Denied = 0. Self-pay, Denial rate = 0.0%. All payers, Claims adjudicated in Q2 = 632. All payers, Denied = 43. All payers, Denial rate = 6.8%\n• System denial rate on claims adjudicated in Q2: 6.8% (43 of 632).\n• Largest denial reason by claim count: Prior authorization missing (12 claims). Prior authorization missing: 12 claims.\n• Appeal windows differ by payer: see the payer contract summary RHN-CON-009. Prior authorization turnarounds are in policy RHN-REV-021.\nRiverside Health Network | Clinical Quality Committee | Synthetic data for demonstration\n6",
